hadiths[26]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23281","Affan narrated to us: Aban al-Attar narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that he gathered his companions and said: Come, I will pray for you the prayer of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And he was a man of the Ash'aris. He said: He called for a basin of water and washed his hands thrice, rinsed and sniffed, washed his face thrice and his arms thrice, wiped his head and ears, and washed his feet. He said: He prayed Zuhr and recited in it the Fatihah of the Book, and uttered twenty-two takbirs."
"23282","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Abi Husayn, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when there was revealed upon him: O you who believe, do not ask about things which, if made manifest to you, will distress you. He said: So we ask him, or he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has servants who are neither prophets nor martyrs, envied by the prophets and martyrs for their seat and nearness to Allah on the Day of Resurrection. He mentioned the hadith at length."
"23283","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us: Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The greatest misappropriation with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is a cubit of land. You find two men as neighbors in land or in a house, and one of them cuts off a cubit from the share of his companion. When he cuts it off, he will be collared with it from seven earths until the Day of Resurrection."
"23284","Waki' narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to me, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, who said: Abu Malik al-Ash'ari said to his people: Shall I not pray for you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He arranged the men in a row, then arranged the boys behind the men, then arranged the women behind the boys."
"23285","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Awf narrated to us, from Abu al-Minhal, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, who said: There was among us, the company of the Ash'aris, a man who had accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and witnessed with him the fine, beautiful battles. Awf said: I thought he is called Malik or Abu Malik. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I know peoples who are neither prophets nor martyrs, envied by the prophets and martyrs for their place with Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"23286","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that he said to his people: Gather, I will pray with you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When they gathered, he said: Is there among you anyone besides you? They said: No, except a sister's son of ours. He said: A sister's son of a people is of them. He called for a basin containing water and performed ablution, rinsed and sniffed, washed his face thrice and his arms thrice, thrice, wiped his head and the tops of his feet. Then he prayed with them and uttered with them twenty-two takbirs, uttering takbir when he prostrated and when he raised his head from prostration, and recited in the two rak'ahs the Fatihah of the Book, and made audible to whoever was next to him."
"23287","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: Safwan narrated to us, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd al-Hadrami, that Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, when death came to him, said: O hearer of the Ash'aris, let the present of you convey to the absent: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The sweetness of the world is the bitterness of the Hereafter, and the bitterness of the world is the sweetness of the Hereafter."
"23288","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us: Hatim ibn Hurayth narrated to me, from Malik ibn Abi Maryam, who said: We were sitting with Rabi'ah al-Jurashi and mentioned tila' in the caliphate of al-Dahhak ibn Qays. While we were thus, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), entered upon us. We said: Mention tila'. We mentioned tila', Zayd ibn al-Hubab said thus, meaning Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Abu Malik al-Ash'ari narrated to me that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Some people of my ummah will drink wine, calling it by other than its name. The one who narrated to me is more truthful than me and than you, and the one who narrated to him is more truthful than him and than me. He said: By Allah, besides Whom there is no god, I heard it from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari; he heard it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He repeated it to him thrice. Al-Dahhak said: Uff, such a drink of the latter age."
"23289","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, that Abu Malik al-Ash'ari said to his people, and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Sa'd, except that he said: And he washed his feet. And he said: And he recited in the first two rak'ahs the Fatihah of the Book, and made audible to whoever was next to him."
"23290","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Aban ibn Yazid informed me, and Affan narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Yazid informed us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Purity is half of faith, and praise be to Allah fills the scale. Affan said: And glory be to Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, fills what is between heaven and earth. Affan said: And glory be to Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and there is no god but Allah. And Affan said: What is between the heavens and the earth. Prayer is a light, charity is a proof, patience is a radiance, and the Quran is a proof for you or against you. All people go out in the morning; a seller of himself, either destroying it or emancipating it."
"23291","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Musa narrated to us: Aban ibn Yazid informed me, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Abi Sallam, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four of Jahiliyyah will not be left: pride in lineage, defamation of ancestry, seeking rain by the stars, and wailing. The wailing woman, if she does not repent before her death, will be raised on the Day of Resurrection with a garment of tar, or a coat of mange."
"23292","Abu Amir narrated to us: Ali, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from Abu Sallam, who said: Abu Malik said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In my ummah are four of Jahiliyyah they will not leave: pride in lineage, seeking rain by the stars, and wailing over the dead. The wailing woman, if she does not repent before she dies, will stand on the Day of Resurrection with garments of tar, then a coat of Hellfire flame will be raised over her."
"23293","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ibn Mu'aniq or Abu Mu'aniq, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise is a chamber whose outside is seen from its inside and whose inside is seen from its outside. Allah prepared it for whoever feeds food, softens speech, continues fasting, and prays while people sleep."
"23294","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram al-Fazari narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm narrated to us that Abu Malik al-Ash'ari gathered his people and said: O company of the Ash'aris, gather and gather your women and children; I will teach you the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which he prayed for us in Madinah. They gathered and gathered their women and children. He performed ablution and showed them how to perform ablution, completing the ablution to its places, until when the shade turned and the shadow declined, he stood and called the adhan. He arranged the men in the nearest row, arranged the boys behind them, and arranged the women behind the boys. Then he called the iqamah, stepped forward, raised his hands and uttered takbir. He recited the Fatihah of the Book and a surah, making them inaudible. Then he uttered takbir and bowed, saying: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, three times. Then he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, and stood upright. Then he uttered takbir and fell prostrating, then uttered takbir and raised his head, then uttered takbir and prostrated, then uttered takbir and rose standing. His takbir in the first rak'ah was six takbirs, and he uttered takbir when he stood to the second rak'ah. When he finished his prayer, he turned to his people with his face and said: Retain my takbir and learn my bowing and prostration, for it is the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which he used to pray for us at this hour of the day. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he finished his prayer, turned to the people with his face and said: O people, hear and understand and know that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has servants who are neither prophets nor martyrs, envied by the prophets and martyrs for their assemblies and nearness to Allah. A bedouin man came from the farthest of the people and beckoned with his hand to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Prophet of Allah, people who are neither prophets nor martyrs, envied by the prophets and martyrs for their assemblies and nearness to Allah, describe them to us, meaning depict them for us. The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was gladdened by the question of the bedouin. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are people from the outskirts of people and the scattered of tribes, between whom no close kinship is joined; they loved one another in Allah and were sincere to one another. Allah will place for them on the Day of Resurrection pulpits of light and seat them upon them, making their faces light and their garments light. People will be frightened on the Day of Resurrection while they will not be frightened. They are the allies of Allah, upon whom there is no fear, nor do they grieve."
"23295","al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Hariz narrated to us, from Habib ibn Ubayd, from Abu Malik Ubayd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as was conveyed to him, prayed for him: O Allah, bless Ubayd Abu Malik and make him above many of the people."
"23296","Affan narrated to us: Aban narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Zayd, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Purity is half of faith, and praise be to Allah fills the scale, and glory be to Allah and praise be to Allah and Allah is Greatest fills what is between heaven and earth. Prayer is a light, charity is a proof, patience is a radiance, and the Quran is a proof for you or against you. All people go out in the morning; a seller of himself, either emancipating it or destroying it."
"23297","Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us: Abu Ishaq Yahya ibn Maymun, meaning al-Attar, narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me: Zayd ibn Sallam narrated to me, from Abu Sallam: Abd al-Rahman al-Ash'ari narrated to him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Purity is half of faith, and he mentioned its like, except that he said: Prayer is a proof and charity is a light."
"23298","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abd Allah informed us: Ma'mar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from his grandfather Mamtur, from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I think him Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I command you with five: I command you with hearing, obedience, unity, migration, and jihad in the cause of Allah. Whoever leaves the unity the measure of a span has removed the yoke of Islam from his head. Whoever calls with the call of Jahiliyyah is a heap of Hell. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, even if he fasts and prays? He said: Yes, even if he fasts and prays, but call yourselves by the name of Allah by which He named you: servants of Allah, Muslims, believers."
"23299","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah, meaning Shayban, and Layth narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to equalize between the four rak'ahs in recitation and standing, making the first rak'ah the longest of them so the people would join, placing the men before the boys, the boys behind them, and the women behind the boys, uttering takbir whenever he prostrated and whenever he raised, and uttering takbir whenever he rose between the two rak'ahs when he was sitting."
"23300","Affan narrated to us: Aban narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Zayd, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four in my ummah of Jahiliyyah they will not leave: pride in lineage, defamation of ancestry, seeking rain by the stars, and wailing. He said: The wailing woman, if she does not repent before her death, will be raised on the Day of Resurrection with garments of tar and a coat of mange."
"23301","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, that he said to his people: Stand, pray so that I may pray for you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So they lined up behind him, and he said takbir, then recited, then said takbir, then bowed, then raised his head, then said takbir, and he did that in all of his prayer."
"23302","Waki' narrated to us, from Sharik, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The greatest misappropriation before Allah on the Day of Resurrection is a cubit of land between two men, or between two partners in a house, so they divide it, then one of them steals from his companion a cubit of land, so he will be collared with it from seven earths."
"23303","Aswad narrated to us, from Sharik, he said: al-Ash'ari, and he said: When he does that, he will be collared with it from seven earths."
"23304","Aswad narrated to us, from Sharik, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir and Abu al-Nadr both narrated to us, they said: al-Ashja'i, or he said: al-Ash'ari."
"23305","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I was told from al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Waqifi, meaning al-Ansari of Banu Waqif, from Qurra ibn Khalid, Budayl narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, he said: Abu Malik al-Ash'ari said: Shall I not tell you of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: And he gave salam to his right and to his left, then he said: And this is the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And he mentioned the hadith."
"23306","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Amr, informed us, and he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: al-Ashja'i."
